 ## Delivery
 
 `estimateDelivery(orderedAt, transitDays)` returns the expected delivery date in Istanbul time.
+
+## Tax
+
+`computeInvoice(lines, { taxRatePercent, discountPercent = 0 })` takes lines of `{ quantity, unitCents }` (a negative quantity is a credit line) and percentages from 0 to 100 with at most two decimals. It returns `{ lines, netCents, discountCents, taxCents, grossCents }`, with the same four amounts for each line.
+
+- The invoice discount is `discountPercent` of the positive line nets, rounded half to even. It is split across the positive lines in proportion to their nets with the largest-remainder method, and ties go to the earlier line. Credit lines get no discount.
+- Each line's tax is `taxRatePercent` of its net minus its discount, rounded half to even (symmetric for negative amounts).
+- All arithmetic is exact integer arithmetic.
